  (text "NEW for the Commander (rev A1): front 'TO BATT' USB-C port and the 5 V source selector.\n\nThe port is a 5 V-only dual-role USB-C port. A pogo-pin-to-USB-C adapter will dock the battery module here.\n* PoE absent : the module (or any USB-C power bank / 5 V charger) sources VBUS_BATT and U81 feeds the board from it.\n* PoE present: U81 keeps the board on PoE; the SoC may turn U82 on to push 5 V out and charge the module.\nEverything that used to hang on VOUT_5V (VCC_SYS, the nine bay switches, the keyboard) now hangs on VCC5V_BUS.\nAUDIT: the battery module is not designed yet - treat CC / SBU / data on this port as a provisional interface." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid "880995b4-6872-550a-87c7-eeac06411f34"))
